COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[225,"§Hud\ndeeds\nPursue Allah's reward in teaching a Muslim to memorize short Surahs.\nCooperate with a charitable organization in doing a good deed without seeking a financial gain in return.\nVisit one of the righteous weak people and give him a gift.\nguid\nCalling to the way of Allah comes with principles and standards that cannot be compromised no matter how easily we deal with the opponents.\nCaring for the weak is one of the reasons for Allah's victory, provision, and protection. Even if the Prophets (p) participated in oppressing the weak, they would not be safe from Allah's punishment, much less anyone else.\nIf punishment comes to defying nations, then no one would be able to stop it.\nrefl\nوَمَآ أَنَا۠ بِطَارِدِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْۚ إِنَّهُم مُّلَٰقُواْ رَبِّهِمۡ وَلَٰكِنِّيٓ أَرَىٰكُمۡ قَوۡمٗا تَجۡهَلُونَ ٢٩\n(And I will not drive away those who believe), this proves that they asked him to drive away the believers. (They will surely meet their Lord), they will go back to their Lord in the Hereafter, and He will recompense those who drove them away. Al-Qurtubi: 11/110.\nTargeting all classes of society is a sign of truthfulness of one who preaches to Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَيَٰقَوۡمِ مَن يَنصُرُنِي مِنَ ٱللَّهِ إِن طَرَدتُّهُمۡۚ\nMeaning: Who would protect me from His punishment, because driving them away would incur a punishment that no one can ward off except Allah. Al-Saadi: 381.\nOne who preaches to Allah cannot dismiss poor people. Explain?\nوَيَٰقَوۡمِ مَن يَنصُرُنِي مِنَ ٱللَّهِ إِن طَرَدتُّهُمۡۚ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٣٠\nMeaning: Who would save me (from Allah), from His punishment, since driving them away is an insult which harms them without justification before Allah, and He does not like offending His allies. Ibn Ashur: 12/56.\nOffending the allies of Allah, even if they were poor, is a major sin. Explain.\nقَالُواْ يَٰنُوحُ قَدۡ جَٰدَلۡتَنَا فَأَكۡثَرۡتَ جِدَٰلَنَا فَأۡتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ٣٢\nReasoning for the religion is commended. That is why Noah (u) and all the Prophets (p) have reasoned with their people until the truth is clear; whoever accepted it, succeeded, and whoever rejected it, lost. But arguing for falsehood to distort the truth is censured, and whoever does it will be denounced in this life and the Hereafter. Al-Qurtubi: 11/105.\nWhat is the censured arguing?\nقَالُواْ يَٰنُوحُ قَدۡ جَٰدَلۡتَنَا فَأَكۡثَرۡتَ جِدَٰلَنَا فَأۡتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ٣٢\nSome arguing is commended, which is when a believer hopes for a fighting disbeliever to accept Islam, as Allah says, (and argue with them in the best manner) [16:125], and other examples. Some arguing is censured; for example, what occurs among Muslims in search of justification for the rules of Sharia, and envisioning what is relayed by Sharia about the power of Allah. The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade that, and it is detested by the scholars. Ibn Atiyah: 3/166.\nWhat is the commended arguing?\nقَاَلَ إنِّمَا يَأتِيكُم به اْللَّهُ إن شَاءَ ومَا أَنتُم بمُعجِزِينَ\n(Then you will not cause [Him] failure), you will have no escape; it is also said that you will not be victorious despite your great number in which they took pride because they filled the land and mountain. Al-Qurtubi: 11/106.\nFor one who deserves to be misguided, does he benefit from admonishment?\nفَلَا تَبۡتَئِسۡ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَفۡعَلُونَ ٣٦\nMeaning: Do not grieve, for We will destroy them and save you; so only then that Noah (u) invoked Allah against them. Al-Baghawi: 2/398.\nWhen did Noah (u) invoke Allah against his people? What lesson do you learn from that?\nwords\nتَزدَرِيDisdain\nأَم يَقُولُونَThey say\nافتَرَاهُHe fabricated it\nفَلا تَبتَئِسDo not grieve\nالفُلكَThe Ark\nبِأَعيُنِنَاUnder Our care and observation"],[226,"§Hud\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you warn against ridiculing scholars, for they are the heirs of the Prophets.\nMaintain the supplication for boarding today.\nGive advice to one who needs it, just like Noah (u) did with his son.\nguid\nKinship and family ties do not benefit one who does not believe in Allah.\nDo not despair if very few accept your advice and most people do not, for the Prophets (p) spent their long lives before you but none believed with them except a few.\nThe means of this life, no matter how great, will not protect a sinner if Allah decrees to punish him.\nrefl\nوَيَصۡنَعُ ٱلۡفُلۡكَ وَكُلَّمَا مَرَّ عَلَيۡهِ مَلَأٞ مِّن قَوۡمِهِۦ سَخِرُواْ مِنۡهُۚ قَالَ إِن تَسۡخَرُواْ مِنَّا فَإِنَّا نَسۡخَرُ مِنكُمۡ كَمَا تَسۡخَرُونَ ٣٨\nHis people used to pass by him while working and ridicule him by saying: \"O Noah, you became a carpenter after your Prophethood.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/399.\nThe high rank of righteous people did not keep the ignorant from ridiculing them. Explain.\nقُلۡنَا ٱحۡمِلۡ فِيهَا مِن كُلّٖ زَوۡجَيۡنِ ٱثۡنَيۡنِ\nTake on board a male and a female from every type of creature, so that different species could survive. Al-Saadi: 382.\nWhy did Allah command Noah (u) to take on board a pair from every species?\nوَمَآ ءَامَنَ مَعَهُۥٓ إِلَّا قَلِيلٞ ٤٠\nThis statement (But none believed with him except a few) gives more information to complete the lesson from the story about the scarcity of the righteous. Ibn Ashur: 12/73.\nThe righteous are a few among their people. Explain.\nوَقَالَ ٱرۡكَبُواْ فِيهَا بِسۡمِ ٱللَّهِ مَجۡرٜىٰهَا وَمُرۡسَىٰهَآۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٤١\nThis verse proves uttering the name of Allah (bismillah) at the beginning of every action. Al-Qurtubi: 11/121.\nWhat is the practical lesson from this verse?\nوَقَالَ ٱرۡكَبُواْ فِيهَا بِسۡمِ ٱللَّهِ مَجۡرٜىٰهَا وَمُرۡسَىٰهَآۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٤١\nConcluding the verse with the mention of Allah's forgiveness and mercy indicates that Allah promised Noah (u) that He would save them due to His forgiveness and mercy. Ibn Ashur: 12/74.\nThe verse concludes with the mention of Allah’s forgiveness and mercy. Why?\nقَالَ سَـَٔاوِيٓ إِلَىٰ جَبَلٖ يَعۡصِمُنِي مِنَ ٱلۡمَآءِۚ قَالَ لَا عَاصِمَ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ مِنۡ أَمۡرِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا مَن رَّحِمَۚ\nNo mountain or anything else can protect anybody; even if he takes all possible measures, he will not be saved if Allah does not save him. Al-Saadi: 382.\nAt the time of crisis, should we rely on causes, or the Lord of causes (Allah)?\nوَنَادَىٰ نُوحٞ رَّبَّهُۥ فَقَالَ رَبِّ إِنَّ ٱبۡنِي مِنۡ أَهۡلِي وَإِنَّ وَعۡدَكَ ٱلۡحَقُّ وَأَنتَ أَحۡكَمُ ٱلۡحَٰكِمِينَ ٤٥ قَالَ يَٰنُوحُ إِنَّهُۥ لَيۡسَ مِنۡ أَهۡلِكَۖ إِنَّهُۥ عَمَلٌ غَيۡرُ صَٰلِحٖۖ\n(And said, \"My Lord, indeed my son is of my family\"), meaning: You promised to save my family and Your promise is the truth that does not fail. Therefore, how can he (my son) be drowned and You are the Most Just of the judges? (Allah said, \"O Noah, he is not of your family\"), meaning: Your son is not of those whom I promised to save; I only promised you that I would save those of your family who believe. For this reason, Allah said, (and your family – except those who have already been decreed [to drown]) Thus, for his son, it had already been decreed that he would be drowned due to his disbelief and his opposition to his father Noah (u). Ibn Kathir: 2/429.\nRelatives will benefit each other in the Hereafter on the condition of Islam. Explain.\nwords\nوَفَارَIt overflowed with water\nالتَّنُّورThe oven\nمَجرَاهَاIts sailing\nوَمُرسَاهَاIts anchorage\nأَقلِعِيWithhold the rain"],[227,"§Hud\ndeeds\nReview your regular supplications as a precaution against containing an error.\nRead the story of Noah (u), then draw three lessons from it.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness as many as seventy times.\nguid\nDo not worry if your supplications for some worldly things were not answered, for that could be best for you.\nPatience and righteousness are two causes for victory over those who wronged you.\nAllah's promise is realized mostly at the end of a period of testing and trials.\nrefl\nقَالَ يَٰنُوحُ إِنَّهُۥ لَيۡسَ مِنۡ أَهۡلِكَۖ\nMost scholars said: He is not of your religion or allegiance. This proves that the ties of religion are stronger than that of kinship. Al-Qurtubi: 11/134.\nWhat is the great principle that we learn from this verse?\nقَالَ يَٰنُوحُ إِنَّهُۥ لَيۡسَ مِنۡ أَهۡلِكَۖ إِنَّهُۥ عَمَلٌ غَيۡرُ صَٰلِحٖۖ فَلَا تَسۡـَٔلۡنِ مَا لَيۡسَ لَكَ بِهِۦ عِلۡمٌۖ\n(So do not ask of Me that of what you have no knowledge), do not ask Me that of which you do not know the outcome, whether it will be good or otherwise. Al-Saadi: 382.\nOne may ask Allah for something, but it is best for him not to get it. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَإِلَّا تَغۡفِرۡ لِي وَتَرۡحَمۡنِيٓ أَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٤٧\nForgiveness and mercy will save a person from being among the losers. Al-Saadi: 383.\nWhat are the causes of being saved in the Hereafter?\nوَإِلَّا تَغۡفِرۡ لِي وَتَرۡحَمۡنِيٓ أَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٤٧\nNoah (u) asked for forgiveness first, then he asked for mercy because once Allah is pleased with him, he will be fit for mercy. Ibn Ashur: 12/88.\nWhy did Noah (u) ask for forgiveness before asking for mercy?\nقِيلَ يَٰنُوحُ ٱهۡبِطۡ بِسَلَٰمٖ مِّنَّا وَبَرَكَٰتٍ عَلَيۡكَ وَعَلَىٰٓ أُمَمٖ مِّمَّن مَّعَكَۚ\nAllah blessed them all until they filled all regions of the earth. Al-Saadi: 383.\nAllah Had blessed the descendants from those who were with Noah (u) in the Ark. What is the indication of that blessing?\nتِلۡكَ مِنۡ أَنۢبَآءِ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ نُوحِيهَآ إِلَيۡكَۖ مَا كُنتَ تَعۡلَمُهَآ أَنتَ وَلَا قَوۡمُكَ مِن قَبۡلِ هَٰذَاۖ فَٱصۡبِرۡۖ إِنَّ ٱلۡعَٰقِبَةَ لِلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٤٩\nMeaning: Just like Noah (u) who was patient, and achieved the best outcome, you [Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ)] will have the best outcome over your people. Ibn Ashur: 12/93.\nAfter the narrative of Noah (u), the Prophet (ﷺ) was commanded to be patient. Why ?\nوَيَٰقَوۡمِ ٱسۡتَغۡفِرُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِ يُرۡسِلِ ٱلسَّمَآءَ عَلَيۡكُم مِّدۡرَارٗا وَيَزِدۡكُمۡ قُوَّةً إِلَىٰ قُوَّتِكُمۡ وَلَا تَتَوَلَّوۡاْ مُجۡرِمِينَ ٥٢\nThis verse proves that asking for Allah's forgiveness and repenting to Him is a cause for rainfall. The repentance mentioned here means repenting from disbelief, then repenting from sins because repentance from sins is valid only after faith. Ibn Juzay: 1/399.\nIdentify some of the benefits of asking for Allah's forgiveness.\nwords\nأَعِظُكَ أَن تَكُونَI admonish you lest you be among the ignorant\nأَعُوذُ بِكَI seek refuge with You\nمُفتَرُونَYou are but fabricators\nمِدرَارًاSuccessive and abundant rain\nعَن قَولِكَOn account of what you say"],[228,"§Hud\ndeeds\nTake Allah as a witness to your disownment from all types of existing shirk.\nIdentify one matter that preoccupied you, and entrust it to Allah while adopting all means, for when He takes your affair into His care, He will suffice you.\nRemind those around you of Allah's favors and His benevolence to them.\nguid\nTrue relying upon Allah instils bravery in the believer's heart.\nRelying upon Allah is a cause for your success in this life and the Hereafter.\nArrogance and stubbornness are two of the worst man's attributes.\nrefl\nفَكِيدُونِي جَمِيعٗا ثُمَّ لَا تُنظِرُونِ ٥٥ إِنِّي تَوَكَّلۡتُ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ رَبِّي وَرَبِّكُمۚ مَّا مِن دَآبَّةٍ إِلَّا هُوَ ءَاخِذُۢ بِنَاصِيَتِهَآۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي عَلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٥٦\nTo be able to say this against so many enemies is indicative of a complete trust in Allah's help. Al-Qurtubi: 11/143.\nWhat does the saying of Hud (u): (So plot against me all together) indicate?\nمَّا مِن دَآبَّةٍ إِلَّا هُوَ ءَاخِذُۢ بِنَاصِيَتِهَآۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي عَلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٥٦\n(There is no moving creature), a soul living on Earth. (But He holds it by its forelock), He has perfect power over it; He can discharge or restrain it. Al-Qurtubi: 11/143.\nThis verse shows an example of Allah's power, and the weakness of the creatures. Explain.\nفَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَقَدۡ أَبۡلَغۡتُكُم مَّآ أُرۡسِلۡتُ بِهِۦٓ إِلَيۡكُمۡۚ وَيَسۡتَخۡلِفُ رَبِّي قَوۡمًا غَيۡرَكُمۡ وَلَا تَضُرُّونَهُۥ شَيۡـًٔاۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٍ حَفِيظٞ ٥٧\n(And you cannot harm Him in the least), by denying and turning away; rather you harm yourselves. It is also said that if He destroys you, that will not diminish anything from His sovereignty because your existence or inexistence are the same to Him. Al-Baghawi: 2/409.\nCan anyone harm his Lord by turning away from His obedience?\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَ أَمۡرُنَا نَجَّيۡنَا هُودٗا وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَعَهُۥ بِرَحۡمَةٖ مِّنَّا وَنَجَّيۡنَٰهُم مِّنۡ عَذَابٍ غَلِيظٖ ٥٨\nNo one can be saved unless by the mercy of Allah, even if he has good deeds. Al-Qurtubi: 11/146.\nCan anyone be saved from Allah’s punishment by his good deeds only?\nوَتِلۡكَ عَادٞۖ جَحَدُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّهِمۡ وَعَصَوۡاْ رُسُلَهُۥ وَٱتَّبَعُوٓاْ أَمۡرَ كُلِّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيدٖ ٥٩\nWhoever disobeys one Messenger, disobeys them all, for they are all in accord on believing in the Oneness of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 1/400.\nThis verse proves that whoever rejects one Messenger, he rejects them all. Explain.\nفَٱسۡتَغۡفِرُوهُ ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي قَرِيبٞ مُّجِيبٞ ٦١\nThis type of closeness leads to the bestowal of Allah's mercy, His response to their supplications and His fulfilment of their hopes. Hence, He mentions His name, (the Near) alongside His name (the Responsive). Al-Saadi: 385.\nAllah joines His Holy Name (the Near) with (the Responsive). Why?\nقَالُواْ يَٰصَٰلِحُ قَدۡ كُنتَ فِينَا مَرۡجُوّٗا قَبۡلَ هَٰذَآۖ\nMeaning: We truly had hopes in you before this, and expected wisdom and benefit from you. This testimony on their part in favor of their Prophet Salih indicates that he was known for his good attitude and noble character, and that he was among the best of his people. Al-Saadi: 385.\nThe scholar who calls to Allah should combine between faith and good morals. Explain.\nwords\nاعتَرَاكَAfflicted you\nفَكِيدُونِيDo your best to cause me harm\nثُمَّ لا تُنظِرُونِThen give me no respite.\nآخِذٌ بِنَاصِيَتِهَاAllah has perfect power over His creation\nوَاستَعمَرَكُم فِيهَاAnd Allah settled you in it [the Earth]\nكُنتَ فِينَا مَرجُوًّاWe had hopes in you to be a leader among us"],[229,"§Hud\ndeeds\nIdentify an evil deed, and forbid it using a wise and convincing approach.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek protection in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek protection in Your forgiveness from Your punishment. and I seek protection in You from You. I cannot enumerate Your praises, You are as You have praised Yourself.\"\nInvite a colleague, who assists you in doing good deed, to your house, and show him hospitality, following the example of Prophet Abraham (u).\nguid\nFor one who calls others to Allah, he must have knowledge of what he is preaching by ascertaining the topics before talking about them.\nThe believer knows that the blessings through which he is living such as guidance, righteousness and piety are all but Allah's favor and mercy.\nWhoever invites you to commit a sin cannot ward off Allah's punishment from you, so remain steadfast in obeying Allah.\nrefl\nوَيَٰقَوۡمِ هَٰذِهِۦ نَاقَةُ ٱللَّهِ لَكُمۡ ءَايَةٗۖ\nThe she-camel is attributed to the Holy Name of Allah because it was created by His mighty power. Ibn Ashur: 12/113.\nWhy is it referred to as: the (she-camel of Allah)?\nفَعَقَرُوهَا فَقَالَ تَمَتَّعُواْ فِي دَارِكُمۡ ثَلَٰثَةَ أَيَّامٖۖ ذَٰلِكَ وَعۡدٌ غَيۡرُ مَكۡذُوبٖ ٦٥\n(But they hamstrung her), she was slaughtered by few, but the action is attributed to all of them because they had consented to it. Al-Qurtubi: 11/154.\nWe may see one who does not do evil, but he is content with it. What is the ruling of Sharia in his case?\nوَأَخَذَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ ٱلصَّيۡحَةُ فَأَصۡبَحُواْ فِي دِيَٰرِهِمۡ جَٰثِمِينَ ٦٧\nAllah called Thamud as: (those who did wrong) to indicate the reason for their destruction which is wrongdoing by associating partners with Allah (shirk). This is also viewed as a warning to the polytheists of Makkah that they could face similar punishment because they were wrongdoers too. Ibn Ashur: 12/114.\nAllah called Thamud as: (those who did wrong). Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ جَآءَتۡ رُسُلُنَآ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ بِٱلۡبُشۡرَىٰ قَالُواْ سَلَٰمٗاۖ\nFrom this, it is learned that greeting should be given before speaking. Al-Saadi: 385.\nWhat do we learn from the greeting of the angels?\nفَمَا لَبِثَ أَن جَآءَ بِعِجۡلٍ حَنِيذٖ ٦٩\nThis verse contains an etiquette of guest hosting by hastening to provide him with the available item of food, and following with another, if any. But the host should not overburden himself with what he cannot afford. Al-Qurtubi: 11/159.\nExplain one of the etiquettes of guest hosting.\nفَلَمَّا رَءَآ أَيۡدِيَهُمۡ لَا تَصِلُ إِلَيۡهِ نَكِرَهُمۡ وَأَوۡجَسَ مِنۡهُمۡ خِيفَةٗۚ قَالُواْ لَا تَخَفۡ إِنَّآ أُرۡسِلۡنَآ إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِ لُوطٖ ٧٠\nQatadah said: They used to think that if a guest does not eat their food, then he does not come with good intention, rather he has evil one. Al-Baghawi: 2/412.\nWhy did Abraham (u) feel scared when the angels did not eat his food?\nإِنَّآ أُرۡسِلۡنَآ إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِ لُوطٖ ٧٠ وَٱمۡرَأَتُهُۥ قَآئِمَةٞ فَضَحِكَتۡ\nWe are sent to the people of Lot in order to destroy them. Then, Sarah laughed in delight of the good news of their destruction because they had excessive corruption, immense disbelief and stubbornness. Ibn Kathir: 2/433.\nWhy was Sarah delighted and laughed when she heard the news from the angels?\nwords\nتَخسِيرٍMisguidance, increase in loss\nفَعَقَرُوهَاThey slaughtered it\nجَاثِمِينَThey became corpses fallen prone\nنَكِرَهُمHe deemed that strange from them"],[230,"§Hud\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah for mercy and guidance of those who went astray.\nLook for good news and share them with those around you to bring them joy.\nSupplicate Allah to grant you forbearance and constant reversion to Him.\nguid\nAllah's Decree is absolute; when it happens, no one can prevent it.\nIf the close friend of the Merciful supplicated Allah, the Almighty, and repented, then why should not we repent and turn to Allah?\nNever despair of begetting righteous descendants.\nrefl\nقَالُوٓاْ أَتَعۡجَبِينَ مِنۡ أَمۡرِ ٱللَّهِۖ\nThere is nothing strange in His decree, for His will is always done. So there is nothing strange about what His might and power may do. Al-Saadi: 386.\nAbraham's wife should not have been amazed by the decree of Allah. Why?\nفَلَمَّا ذَهَبَ عَنۡ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ ٱلرَّوۡعُ وَجَآءَتۡهُ ٱلۡبُشۡرَىٰ يُجَٰدِلُنَا فِي قَوۡمِ لُوطٍ ٧٤\nThe argument of Abraham (u) with the angels is described in this verse as pleading with Allah since Abraham (u) wanted to ward off a decree by Allah to punish the people of Lot (u). Ibn Ashur: 12/123.\nThe argument was with the angels, but it is described as pleading with Allah. Why?\nإِنَّ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ لَحَلِيمٌ أَوَّٰهٞ مُّنِيبٞ ٧٥\n(Abraham was indeed forbearing), he had a good attitude and was patient and big-hearted; he did not get angry with the ignorance of the ignorant. (Tenderhearted), he would humbly beseech Allah at all times. (And constantly returning in repentance), he constantly turned back to Allah by knowing Him and loving Him, and by turning to Him and turning away from all others but Him. Hence, he argued on behalf of those whom Allah decreed were to be destroyed. Al-Saadi: 386.\nWhat are the prominent traits of Abraham (u), so we emulate him?\nإِنَّ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ لَحَلِيمٌ أَوَّٰهٞ مُّنِيبٞ ٧٥\n(Constantly returning in repentance), the one who reverts to Allah, and Abraham (u) was always reverting to Allah, the Almighty in all of his affairs. (Tenderhearted), the one who felt a great regret over the people of Lot (u) for missing the faith in Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 11/173.\nThe Prophets' mercy for their people causes them to be distressed over their punishment. Explain.\nفَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَلَا تُخۡزُونِ فِي ضَيۡفِيٓۖ أَلَيۡسَ مِنكُمۡ رَجُلٞ رَّشِيدٞ ٧٨\nThis question (Is there not a right-minded man among you?) is a scathing rebuke to them because insulting a guest is a disgraceful act which is done only by the foolish. Ibn Ashur: 12/129.\nWhat is the aim of this question: (Is there not a right-minded man among you)?\nأَلَيۡسَ مِنكُمۡ رَجُلٞ رَّشِيدٞ ٧٨\nMeaning: A strong man enjoins what is right and forbids what is evil. Right-mindedness is guidance and straightness. Al-Qurtubi: 11/173.\nWhat are the traits of the right-minded man?\nقَالُواْ يَٰلُوطُ إِنَّا رُسُلُ رَبِّكَ لَن يَصِلُوٓاْ إِلَيۡكَۖ فَأَسۡرِ بِأَهۡلِكَ بِقِطۡعٖ مِّنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَلَا يَلۡتَفِتۡ مِنكُمۡ أَحَدٌ إِلَّا ٱمۡرَأَتَكَۖ إِنَّهُۥ مُصِيبُهَا مَآ أَصَابَهُمۡۚ إِنَّ مَوۡعِدَهُمُ ٱلصُّبۡحُۚ أَلَيۡسَ ٱلصُّبۡحُ بِقَرِيبٖ ٨١\nThey were forbidden from looking back so that they would not feel sorrow for their hometown. Ibn Juzay: 1/403.\nAllah forbade His Messenger Lot (u) and his family from looking back. Why?\nwords\nبَعلِيMy husband\nالرَّوعُThe shock of fear\nأَوَّاهٌHe supplicates with humility, tenderhearted\nمُنِيبٌHe is constantly returning in repentance\nسِيءَ بِهِمHe was anguished for them\nوَضَاقَ بِهِم ذَرعًاHe felt for them great discomfort\nعَصِيبٌA distressing\nيُهرَعُونThey came hastening"],[231,"§Hud\ndeeds\nReckon with yourself, whether you have wronged someone in matters of honor, money or anything else, then return the rights to their rightful owners.\nIdentify a good deed, learn its Sharia rules, implement it, then invite those around you to partake in it.\nWhenever you are doing something today, begin by saying: \"O Allah, grant me success toward what You love and accept.\"\nguid\nMajor sins are not alike, some are more severely punished than others.\nA small lawful profit is better and more blessed than a large unlawful one.\nWhoever wants to call others to doing good deeds, should have clear knowledge and understanding of what he is preaching.\nrefl\nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِندَ رَبِّكَۖ وَمَا هِيَ مِنَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ بِبَعِيدٖ ٨٣\nMeaning: O Muhammad, these stones are not far from the evildoers among your people. Qatadah and Ikrimah said: This means that the evildoers among the Muslims; by Allah, He does not exclude any wrongdoer. Al-Qurtubi: 11/189.\nAre these divine punishments exclusive to the people of Lot (u), or they can strike evildoers at any time?\nوَلَا تَنقُصُواْ ٱلۡمِكۡيَالَ وَٱلۡمِيزَانَۖ إِنِّيٓ أَرَىٰكُم بِخَيۡرٖ\nIn addition to their disbelief, they were defrauders. When a seller came to them with food, they took full weight as much as they could, and did him wrong. When a buyer came to purchase food, they gave him less weight as much as they could. Al-Qurtubi: 11/191.\nWhat is the risk in defrauding people out of their provisions and livelihood? How was it a cause for punishment?\nبَقِيَّتُ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَۚ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ عَلَيۡكُم بِحَفِيظٖ ٨٦\nMeaning: Whatever profit that remains for you after fulfilling the rights of others is more blessed and indeed better than the fraudulent gain that you keep for yourselves through acts of tyranny and wrongdoing. Al-Qurtubi: 11/192.\nWhich one matters: the abundance of money or its blessed nature? Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالُواْ يَٰشُعَيۡبُ أَصَلَوٰتُكَ تَأۡمُرُكَ أَن نَّتۡرُكَ مَا يَعۡبُدُ ءَابَآؤُنَآ أَوۡ أَن نَّفۡعَلَ فِيٓ أَمۡوَٰلِنَا مَا نَشَٰٓؤُاْۖ إِنَّكَ لَأَنتَ ٱلۡحَلِيمُ ٱلرَّشِيدُ ٨٧\nThey said that by way of mocking him and meaning the opposite of what they said, but he was not as they thought he was. Rather, he was as they said, his prayer did teach him that he should tell them not to worship that which their misguided forefathers had worshiped, and not to do whatever they pleased with that wealth, for prayer restrains one from shameful and evil acts, and what acts can be more shameful and evil than worshiping something other than Allah, withholding people's dues, or stealing by giving short weight and measure? Shu’ayb was indeed the forbearing and right-minded one. Al-Saadi: 387.\nThe verse mentions one of the aims of prayer. Explain.\nقَالُواْ يَٰشُعَيۡبُ أَصَلَوٰتُكَ تَأۡمُرُكَ أَن نَّتۡرُكَ مَا يَعۡبُدُ ءَابَآؤُنَآ أَوۡ أَن نَّفۡعَلَ فِيٓ أَمۡوَٰلِنَا مَا نَشَٰٓؤُاْۖ إِنَّكَ لَأَنتَ ٱلۡحَلِيمُ ٱلرَّشِيدُ ٨٧\nAmong Shu'ayb's (u) deeds, the prayer was the most distinctive, and therefore, they tied it to anything he would convey to them which went against their norms. Ibn Ashur: 12/141.\nThe Prophets (p) commitment to the prayer made it an influential act of worship in the all aspects of their lives. Explain.\nوَمَآ أُرِيدُ أَنۡ أُخَالِفَكُمۡ إِلَىٰ مَآ أَنۡهَىٰكُمۡ عَنۡهُۚ إِنۡ أُرِيدُ إِلَّا ٱلۡإِصۡلَٰحَ مَا ٱسۡتَطَعۡتُۚ\nMeaning: I cannot forbid you from doing something while I do it, and I do not fail to follow what I enjoin you with. (I only intend reform as much as I am able), I only want to put things right; that you reform your worldly life with justice, and reform your life in the Hereafter with worship. Al-Qurtubi: 11/198.\nThis verse mentions (reform), how is it achieved?\nإِنۡ أُرِيدُ إِلَّا ٱلۡإِصۡلَٰحَ مَا ٱسۡتَطَعۡتُۚ وَمَا تَوۡفِيقِيٓ إِلَّا بِٱللَّهِۚ\n(I only intend reform as much as I am able), because what he said could have been taken as a form of self-praise, he balanced it by saying, (and my success only comes through Allah), whatever I succeed in doing good and whatever I manage to keep away from evil is only by the help of Allah and not by my own strength and power. Al-Saadi: 387.\nAfter telling them that he intended reform, he said, (my success only comes through Allah). Why?\nwords\nسِجِّيلٍStones of baked clay\nمَنضُودٍRaining in close succession\nمُسَوَّمَةًMarked from Allah, like no other on earth\nبَقِيَّتُ اللَّهِWhat remains as lawful profit from Allah"],[232,"§Hud\ndeeds\nRemind those around you that Allah does not make an exception for anyone.\nRead the master supplication for seeking forgiveness as a part of morning and evening remembrance of Allah.\nInvoke Allah by His names (the Merciful) and (the Affectionate), so that He may open many doors of goodness for you.\nguid\nDo not let your problems with certain preachers or righteous people become a ploy for satan to get you to abandon righteousness and worship.\nThe escalation of crises is a sign of their imminent abatement.\nThe fact that Pharaoh's people followed him despite his ignorance and arrogance is proof of the intensity of the trial of the followers. Let the right evidence be your guide, not just words of men.\nrefl\nوَيَٰقَوۡمِ لَا يَجۡرِمَنَّكُمۡ شِقَاقِيٓ أَن يُصِيبَكُم مِّثۡلُ مَآ أَصَابَ قَوۡمَ نُوحٍ أَوۡ قَوۡمَ هُودٍ أَوۡ قَوۡمَ صَٰلِحٖۚ\nWe learn many lessons from Shu'ayb's story; the stories of warnings of punishment and what happened to the earlier generations should be remembered, and these stories, which tell of the punishments that befell the evildoers, should be mentioned in the context of exhortation and admonition. We should also mention the honors that Allah bestowed upon those who feared Him when encouraging and urging people to fear Allah. Al-Saadi: 389.\nThis verse presents an approach used by Shu'ayb (u) when calling his people to Allah, what is it?\nوَٱسۡتَغۡفِرُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي رَحِيمٞ وَدُودٞ ٩٠\n(The Affectionate) has two meanings, one of them is the One Who loves the believers. It is also said that He is the One Who is loved by the believers. Al-Baghawi: 2/421.\nWhat is the meaning of (The Affectionate)? What lesson is learned from this verse?\nقَالُواْ يَٰشُعَيۡبُ مَا نَفۡقَهُ كَثِيرٗا مِّمَّا تَقُولُ وَإِنَّا لَنَرَىٰكَ فِينَا ضَعِيفٗاۖ وَلَوۡلَا رَهۡطُكَ لَرَجَمۡنَٰكَۖ وَمَآ أَنتَ عَلَيۡنَا بِعَزِيزٖ ٩١ قَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ أَرَهۡطِيٓ أَعَزُّ عَلَيۡكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَٱتَّخَذۡتُمُوهُ وَرَآءَكُمۡ ظِهۡرِيًّاۖ\nTheir disparagement of Allah's Messenger is like that of Allah, the Almighty. That is why he said, (does my clan have a higher status to you than Allah. And you have abandoned Him behind your backs). Ibn Juzay: 1/404.\nThe belittlement of a scholar or a preacher for his religion is like that of Allah, the Almighty. Explain.\nقَالُواْ يَٰشُعَيۡبُ مَا نَفۡقَهُ كَثِيرٗا مِّمَّا تَقُولُ\nThat was because of their resentment and aversion toward what he said. Al-Saadi: 388.\nWhat is the reason preventing them from understanding Shu'ayb (u)?\nوَلَوۡلَا رَهۡطُكَ لَرَجَمۡنَٰكَۖ وَمَآ أَنتَ عَلَيۡنَا بِعَزِيزٖ ٩١\nAllah protects the believers by many means, some of which they may be aware of and others they may know nothing of. He may protect them by means of their tribe or their fellow countrymen who are disbelievers, as Allah protected Shu'ayb from the stoning of his people by means of his family. There is nothing wrong with benefiting from these ties, by means of which Islam and Muslims may be protected; indeed, that may be a must, because putting things right is required to the extent of one’s ability and what is possible. Al-Saadi: 389.\nIs it permitted for a Muslim to pursue worldly means to protect his religion?\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَ أَمۡرُنَا نَجَّيۡنَا شُعَيۡبٗا وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَعَهُۥ بِرَحۡمَةٖ مِّنَّا وَأَخَذَتِ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ ٱلصَّيۡحَةُ فَأَصۡبَحُواْ فِي دِيَٰرِهِمۡ جَٰثِمِينَ ٩٤\nHere, Allah mentions that a huge blast (Sayhah) came to them. In Surat Al-A'raf, He says a severe quake (Rajfah) came to them. In Surat Ash-Shu'ara', He said it was a torment of a cloudy day. They were one nation upon which all of these punishments were gathered on the day of their destruction. In each context, Allah mentioned what was suitable. Ibn Kathir: 2/439.\nAllah mentions three types of punishments for people of Shu'ayb. How do you reconcile these verses?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا مُوسَىٰ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا وَسُلۡطَٰنٖ مُّبِينٍ ٩٦ إِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَمَلَإِيْهِۦ\nMeaning: The nobles of his people, because they were the ones who were followed; other people would follow their lead. Al-Saadi: 389.\nThe nobles of the Pharaoh are singled out for mention, even though Moses (u) was sent to all the people of the Pharaoh. Why?\nwords\nلا يَجرِمَنَّكُمDo not let it cause you\nشِقَاقِيYour dissension from me\nرَهطُكَYour clan\nوَرَاءَكُم ظِهرِيًّاBehind your backs\nمَكَانَتِكُمAccording to your position"],[233,"§Hud\ndeeds\nRead one of the narrations in the Quran while reflecting and drawing lessons from it.\nRead Surat Yusuf (u) while reflecting on the wrong done by individuals, and read Surat Hud (u), reflecting on the wrong done by people of the cities; then ask refuge with Allah from both.\nRecite some verses of the Quran, from the verses of warning, and ask Allah to make you fearful of Him.\nguid\nA befitting recompense. Just as the tyrant precedes his people in falsehood in this world, he will precede them to Hellfire in the Hereafter.\nAllah, the Almighty, is exalted above wronging people when it comes to destroying polytheists and the sinners.\nThe narrations of the Quran are not for pastime, but for reminding and admonishing.\nrefl\nيَقۡدُمُ قَوۡمَهُۥ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ فَأَوۡرَدَهُمُ ٱلنَّارَۖ وَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡوِرۡدُ ٱلۡمَوۡرُودُ ٩٨\nHe will be at the forefront of his people to Hellfire since he was their leader. Al-Qurtubi: 11/204.\nWhoever leads people to evil in this life, will lead them to Hellfire on the Day of Resurrection. Explain.\nيَقۡدُمُ قَوۡمَهُۥ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ فَأَوۡرَدَهُمُ ٱلنَّارَۖ وَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡوِرۡدُ ٱلۡمَوۡرُودُ ٩٨\nJust as they followed him in this life and he was their leader and chief, likewise he will lead them to Hellfire on the Day of Resurrection. He will lead them directly to it, where they will drink from springs of destruction. Pharaoh will have a great share in that awful punishment. Ibn Kathir: 2/440.\nWhy will Pharaoh be at forefront of his people on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَمَا ظَلَمۡنَٰهُمۡ وَلَٰكِن ظَلَمُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡۖ\n(But they wronged themselves), they wronged themselves with disbelief and disobedience. Al-Baghawi: 2/423.\nHow does one wrong himself?\nفَمَآ أَغۡنَتۡ عَنۡهُمۡ ءَالِهَتُهُمُ ٱلَّتِي يَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مِن شَيۡءٖ لَّمَّا جَآءَ أَمۡرُ رَبِّكَۖ\nThis applies to everyone who turns to other than Allah; it does not avail them anything when calamity strikes. Al-Saadi: 389.\nWhat is the outcome for one who turns to other than Allah?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَخۡذُ رَبِّكَ إِذَآ أَخَذَ ٱلۡقُرَىٰ وَهِيَ ظَٰلِمَةٌۚ إِنَّ أَخۡذَهُۥٓ أَلِيمٞ شَدِيدٌ ١٠٢\nEven when the lying wicked are given authority, it will, inevitably, disappear, and only their disgrace and infamy will remain; their rise and fall happen very fast. Ibn Taimyah: 3/557.\nIn light of this verse, how does Allah punish wicked cities?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ شَقُواْ فَفِي ٱلنَّارِ لَهُمۡ فِيهَا زَفِيرٞ وَشَهِيقٌ ١٠٦\nOf their torments in Hellfire, Allah singles out for mention exhaling and inhaling to repel people from that which lead to Hellfire because the deformation caused by exhaling and inhaling is more frightening than the pain. Ibn Ashur: 12/165.\nAllah singles out for mention exhaling and inhaling. Why?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ شَقُواْ فَفِي ٱلنَّارِ لَهُمۡ فِيهَا زَفِيرٞ وَشَهِيقٌ ١٠٦\nExhaling is a sound in the throat and inhaling is a sound in the chest. This means that their exhaling will be \"Zafir\" and their inhaling will be \"Shahiq.\" This will be due to the torment that they will be experiencing. We seek refuge with Allah from such evil. Ibn Kathir: 2/441.\nWhat is the aim for describing the people of Hellfire as having \"Zafir\" and \"Shahiq\"?\nwords\nفَأَورَدَهُمHe led them\nالمَورُودA place to be led to [Hellfire]\nالرِّفدُThe gift\nالمَرفُودُWhich is given\nوَحَصِيدٌMowed down with nothing left"],[234,"§Hud\ndeeds\nLook for a righteous company to be with today, and do not incline to the defiantly disobedient and the wrongdoers, lest you be gathered with them on the Last Day.\nMaintain with care all daily prayers on time and in congregation, especially Al-Fajr and Al-Asr prayers.\nDenounce, in a wise manner, the religious innovators and those who commit sins openly.\nguid\nA person is not on the right course of Islam unless he is in accord with the Quran and Sunnah, and disregards his whims.\nKeep away from doing wrong and the wrongdoers, as much as possible.\nIndulging in luxury and pleasures is a cause for misguidance.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَى ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ فَٱخۡتُلِفَ فِيهِۚ\nIf this was their attitude toward their own Scripture, then it should come as no surprise that the Jews would not believe in the Quran which Allah has revealed to you, and would have grave doubt concerning it. Al-Saadi: 390.\nThose who cast doubts about the Quran resemble the Jews. Explain.\nفَٱسۡتَقِمۡ كَمَآ أُمِرۡتَ وَمَن تَابَ مَعَكَ\nAllah, the Exalted, commands His Messenger and His believing servants to be firm on the right course. For this is one of the greatest aids for gaining victory over the enemy and confronting the opposition. Ibn Kathir: 2/443.\nAfter mentioning those who opposed the Prophet (ﷺ), Allah mentions His command to be firm on the right course. Why?\nوَلَا تَرۡكَنُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ فَتَمَسَّكُمُ ٱلنَّارُ وَمَا لَكُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مِنۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ ثُمَّ لَا تُنصَرُونَ ١١٣\nIbn Abbas (t) said: \"Do not lean\", inclining is liking them, and leaning is by heart. Abu Al-Aliyah said: \"Do not be content with what they do.\" Al-Suddi said: \"Do not compromise with the wrongdoers.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/428.\nWhat is the sign of inclining toward the wrongdoers?\nوَلَا تَرۡكَنُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ فَتَمَسَّكُمُ ٱلنَّارُ\nThis indicates abandoning the disbelievers and wrongdoers such as the religious innovators and others, since being in their company may lead to disbelief, for true friendship comes as a result of affection. Al-Qurtubi: 11/226.\nWhat is the duty of the believer when it comes to selecting friends and companions?\nوَلَا تَرۡكَنُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ فَتَمَسَّكُمُ ٱلنَّارُ وَمَا لَكُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مِنۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ ثُمَّ لَا تُنصَرُونَ ١١٣\nIf this warning has to do with inclining toward the wrongdoers, then what about the wrongdoers themselves? We ask Allah to keep us safe and sound from wrongdoing. Al-Saadi: 391.\nThis verse contains a great warning to the wrongdoers. How can we infer that?\nوَأَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ طَرَفَيِ ٱلنَّهَارِ وَزُلَفٗا مِّنَ ٱلَّيۡلِۚ إِنَّ ٱلۡحَسَنَٰتِ يُذۡهِبۡنَ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِۚ ذَٰلِكَ ذِكۡرَىٰ لِلذَّٰكِرِينَ ١١٤\nThe prayer is mentioned here since it is the second pillar of Islam, and it is the one thing that Muslims turn to during crisis. Moreover, when anything distressed the Prophet (ﷺ) he hastened to the prayer. Al-Qurtubi: 11/227.\nExplain the great importance of the prayer in light of this verse.\nوَٱصۡبِرۡ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجۡرَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١١٥\nAfter commanding them to be firm on the right course and not incline toward the wrongdoers, Allah commands them to be patient since observing these commands entails great hardship and they go against the desires of many people. So, it is fitting to command patience with all hardships, as suitable to each. Ibn Ashur: 12/182.\nAllah commands patience after His command to be firm on the right course. Why?\nwords\nتَكُDo no be\nمِريَةٍDoubt\nوَلا تَطغَواAnd do not transgress\nوَلا تَركَنُواAnd do not incline\nأُولُو بَقِيَّةٍRighteous people still remaining\nأُترِفُوا فِيهِThey pursued their luxury"],[235,"§Hud, Yusuf\ndeeds\nReconcile between two differing individuals today. Discord is a natural phenomena while harmony is an Islamic Sunnah.\nThink of a matter that worries you, and say, \"Allah suffices me, there is none worthy of worship but Him. I have placed my trust in Him, He is Lord of the Majestic Throne.\"\nDivide Surat Yusuf into sections, then practice giving talks about them to students for the sake of admonishing and reminding.\nguid\nKeep away from what causes differences and dispute, and let your aim be gathering with the believers and the righteous around Sunnah and Jama'ah.\nBenefiting from the Quran can be attained through listening and the will to learn.\nGood story telling is a successful educational and teaching approach.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ لَجَعَلَ ٱلنَّاسَ أُمَّةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗۖ وَلَا يَزَالُونَ مُخۡتَلِفِينَ ١١٨ إِلَّا مَن رَّحِمَ رَبُّكَۚ وَلِذَٰلِكَ خَلَقَهُمۡۗ وَتَمَّتۡ كَلِمَةُ رَبِّكَ لَأَمۡلَأَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنَ ٱلۡجِنَّةِ وَٱلنَّاسِ أَجۡمَعِينَ ١١٩\nAllah states that the people of mercy do not differ with each other; they are the followers of the Prophets in words and in deeds, and they are the people of Quran and Hadith in this Muslim nation. Whoever differs with them, will miss a share in mercy that is equivalent to the extent of his difference with them. Hence, since philosophers are the furthest away from following the Prophets, they are in extreme difference with each other. These sects: Khawarij, Mu'tazila, and Shiats are far way from Sunnah and Hadith, and therefore, they are in great differences, especially Shiats who, of all sects, have the most differences because they are the furthest away from the people of Sunnah. Ibn Taimyah: 3/562.\nThe verse indicates that people of Sunnah are less likely to differ with each other, and the people of religious innovation are in extreme difference with each other. How?\nوَكُلّٗا نَّقُصُّ عَلَيۡكَ مِنۡ أَنۢبَآءِ ٱلرُّسُلِ مَا نُثَبِّتُ بِهِۦ فُؤَادَكَۚ\nSo that your heart may be reassured and made steadfast and patient, as the Messengers of firm resolve were patient, because hearts feel at ease when they have an example to follow, they will be energized to do righteous deeds, and will want to compete in doing them. So, the truth is supported by mentioning the proofs thereof and the large number of people who follow it. Al-Saadi: 392.\nWhich aspects of the stories that make the heart steadfast and reassured?\nوَلِلَّهِ غَيۡبُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَإِلَيۡهِ يُرۡجَعُ ٱلۡأَمۡرُ كُلُّهُۥ فَٱعۡبُدۡهُ وَتَوَكَّلۡ عَلَيۡهِۚ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَٰفِلٍ عَمَّا تَعۡمَلُونَ ١٢٣\nReliance upon Allah and seeking His help is an act of worship, but it is singled out for mention so that the worshiper focuses on it. It is the driving force behind performing all acts of worship since Allah cannot be worshiped without His help. Ibn Taimyah: 3/563.\nReliance upon Allah is singled out for mention even though it is an act of worship. Why?\nإِنَّآ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ قُرۡءَٰنًا عَرَبِيّٗا لَّعَلَّكُمۡ تَعۡقِلُونَ ٢\nThe Arabic language is the most eloquent, plain, deep and expressive of the meanings that might arise in one's mind. Therefore, the most honorable Book, was revealed in the most honorable language. Ibn Kathir: 2/448.\nWhy was the Quran revealed in the Arabic language?\nإِنَّآ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ قُرۡءَٰنًا عَرَبِيّٗا لَّعَلَّكُمۡ تَعۡقِلُونَ ٢\nThe most honorable Book, was revealed in the most honorable language, to the most honorable Prophet and Messenger (ﷺ) delivered by the most honorable angel, in the most honorable land on earth, and its revelation started during the most honorable month of the year, Ramadan. Therefore, the Quran is perfect in every respect. Ibn Kathir: 2/448.\nThe Quran is honored in many aspects. What are they?\nنَحۡنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيۡكَ أَحۡسَنَ ٱلۡقَصَصِ\nThis story is one of the best and clearest of stories, because it moves from one situation to another, from trial to trial, from trial to blessing, from humiliation to honor, from slavery to a position of authority, from separation and fragmentation to reunion and harmony, from sorrow to joy, from ease to hardship, from hardship to ease, from restriction to abundance, and from denial to admission. Al-Saadi: 407.\nWhy is the story of Joseph (u) one of the best of stories?\nنَحۡنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيۡكَ أَحۡسَنَ ٱلۡقَصَصِ\nIt should be noted that Allah states that He tells His Messenger (ﷺ) the best of stories in this Book, then He tells this story and explains it, and tells what happened. Thus, it is known that it is a complete, perfect and beautiful story. Whoever wants to augment it or improve on it by narrating what is mentioned in the Jewish sources (Israeliyat) that have no known chain of narration or narrator, and most of which are false, thinks he is filling so-called gaps in the story that Allah revealed, and he is trying to perfect something that he claims is lacking. Al-Saadi: 393.\nWhat do you think of those who add to the story of Joseph (u) what is not narrated in Quran or Sunnah?\nwords\nأُمَّةً وَاحِدَةًOne nation with one religion which is Islam\nمَكَانَتِكُمYour way, position\nلَمِنَ الغَافِلِينَYou were unaware of their stories"],[236,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nRead the Prophet's (ﷺ) Hadiths in interpreting dreams of his Companions (j).\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil eye and envy, since they are sources of many trials.\nDenounce an evil intention or act on which your relatives or friends agreed.\nguid\nIt is wise to conceal your plans from those who are suspected of jealousy or envy.\nJealousy is a natural tendency, but if one accepts it, then the devil would use it to steer him toward envy and committing a crime.\nNo one can be blamed for loving his son.\nrefl\nقَالَ يَٰبُنَيَّ لَا تَقۡصُصۡ رُءۡيَاكَ عَلَىٰٓ إِخۡوَتِكَ فَيَكِيدُواْ لَكَ كَيۡدًاۖ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ لِلۡإِنسَٰنِ عَدُوّٞ مُّبِينٞ ٥\n(Do not relate your vision to your brothers), this is said by father of Joseph (u) because he knew that Joseph's vision meant he would attain high rank in life, so his father was worried about him being envied by his brothers. Ibn Juzay: 1/410.\nThe verse indicates a way to guard oneself against envy. What is it?\nقَالَ يَٰبُنَيَّ لَا تَقۡصُصۡ رُءۡيَاكَ عَلَىٰٓ إِخۡوَتِكَ فَيَكِيدُواْ لَكَ كَيۡدًاۖ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ لِلۡإِنسَٰنِ عَدُوّٞ مُّبِينٞ ٥\nFrom this, one should hide the prospects or the coming of a bounty until it comes into existence and becomes known. Ibn Kathir: 2/450.\nIf Allah grants you a bounty, when should you expose it? When should you hide it?\nقَالَ يَٰبُنَيَّ لَا تَقۡصُصۡ رُءۡيَاكَ عَلَىٰٓ إِخۡوَتِكَ فَيَكِيدُواْ لَكَ كَيۡدًاۖ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ لِلۡإِنسَٰنِ عَدُوّٞ مُّبِينٞ ٥\nIn authentic Hadith, it is narrated that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"When one of you sees a dream that he likes, then it is from Allah; he should praise Allah for it and relate it to [others]. And if he sees one which he dislikes, then it is from satan; he should seek refuge with Allah against its evil and should not mention it to anyone, for it will not harm him.\" Jabir (t) reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"When one of you sees a bad dream let him blow three times on his left, seek refuge with Allah from satan three times, and change the side on which he was lying.\" Al-Alusi: 12/514.\nWhat is the guidance of the Prophet (ﷺ) in dealing with dreams?\nلَّقَدۡ كَانَ فِي يُوسُفَ وَإِخۡوَتِهِۦٓ ءَايَٰتٞ لِّلسَّآئِلِينَ ٧\nFor everyone who shows interest and asks, as those who enquire are the ones who benefit from the signs and lessons. As for those who turn away, they will not benefit from signs, stories or explanations. Al-Saadi: 394.\nThose who ask are singled out to benefit from the signs. Why?\nٱقۡتُلُواْ يُوسُفَ أَوِ ٱطۡرَحُوهُ أَرۡضٗا يَخۡلُ لَكُمۡ وَجۡهُ أَبِيكُمۡ وَتَكُونُواْ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ قَوۡمٗا صَٰلِحِينَ ٩\nTheir plot is a sign of low morals, which is eliminating the contest against the best by killing him. This is the most heinous crime because it involves envy, causing harm to others, and violating Allah's command of preserving human soul. But they were religious individuals who were raised in a house of Prophethood, and Allah reformed their lives afterward and called them \"Al-Asbat.\" Ibn Ashur: 12/223.\nThe attitude of Joseph's brothers was an example of how far envy can lead a person. Explain the lesson learned.\nٱقۡتُلُواْ يُوسُفَ أَوِ ٱطۡرَحُوهُ أَرۡضٗا يَخۡلُ لَكُمۡ وَجۡهُ أَبِيكُمۡ وَتَكُونُواْ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ قَوۡمٗا صَٰلِحِينَ ٩\nThey had the intention of repentance before committing the sin, so as to make it easy for them to do it, and reduce the impact of its abhorrent nature, and so that they would encourage one another. Al-Saadi: 394.\nThe verse mentions a trick of satan that he uses against righteous people. What is it?\nٱقۡتُلُواْ يُوسُفَ أَوِ ٱطۡرَحُوهُ أَرۡضٗا يَخۡلُ لَكُمۡ وَجۡهُ أَبِيكُمۡ وَتَكُونُواْ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ قَوۡمٗا صَٰلِحِينَ ٩\nOne sin may lead to many other sins; one sin cannot be committed unless many others were committed before it. When the brothers of Joseph wanted to separate him from his father, they used various kinds of tricks to achieve that; they told lies on several occasions, and they forged the evidence of the bloodstained shirt and came at nightfall weeping in order to deceive their father. Al-Saadi: 408.\nOne sin may lead to many other sins. Discuss this in light of this verse.\nwords\nيَجتَبِيكَHe chooses you\nعُصبَةٌA group of so many\nغَيَابَةِ الجُبِّThe bottom of the well\nيَرتَعHe eats well\nعُصبَةٌA strong group"],[237,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from lying.\nIdentify a matter of concern to you, and bear it with beautiful patience, then do not follow that with a complaint, a blame or harm, so that Allah may relieves your concern.\nSupplicate Allah often today by saying: \"My Lord, increase my knowledge.\"\nguid\nBeware of lying in any situation.\nStrong belief in destiny brings on patience at the time of crisis.\nExcellence in worship is a reason for Allah's protection, help and empowerment.\nrefl\nوَجَآءُوٓ أَبَاهُمۡ عِشَآءٗ يَبۡكُونَ ١٦\nThe insightful mind of a judge is not deceived by such tricks upon which no judgment will be based. As judgment can be based only on evidence. Ibn Ashur: 12/236.\nA judge should not be deceived by tears alone, rather he must ask for a proof. Explain.\nقَالَ بَلۡ سَوَّلَتۡ لَكُمۡ أَنفُسُكُمۡ أَمۡرٗاۖ\nYour souls made fair-seeming to you an abhorrent deed in order to separate me and him. For he realized, from the circumstantial evidence and from the dream that Joseph had told him about, that which proved his suspicion. Al-Saadi: 395.\nWhat was the evidence that showed Joseph's brothers as liars?\nفَصَبۡرٞ جَمِيلٞۖ\nSufyan Al-Thawri said: \"Three qualities are akin to patience: Do not talk about your pain, nor your hardships, and do not claim purity for yourself.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/453.\nIdentify some types of beautiful patience.\nفَصَبۡرٞ جَمِيلٞۖ وَٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُسۡتَعَانُ عَلَىٰ مَا تَصِفُونَ ١٨\n(Beautiful patience) is patience without complaint. Jacob (ﷺ) said, (I only complain of my suffering and my grief to Allah) with saying, (But I will bear it with beautiful patience. It is Allah's help that I seek against what you claim). Thus, complaining to Allah does not contradict beautiful patience. Ibn Taimyah: 4/22.\nWhat is the beautiful patience? Does complaining to Allah contradict that?\nوَجَآءَتۡ سَيَّارَةٞ فَأَرۡسَلُواْ وَارِدَهُمۡ فَأَدۡلَىٰ دَلۡوَهُۥۖ قَالَ يَٰبُشۡرَىٰ هَٰذَا غُلَٰمٞۚ وَأَسَرُّوهُ بِضَٰعَةٗۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمُۢ بِمَا يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٩\n(But Allah is All-Knowing of what they did), Allah knew what Joseph's brothers and those who bought him did. He was able to stop them and prevent them from doing that, but out of His perfect wisdom He decreed otherwise. He let them do what they did, so that His decision prevails and His appointed destiny rules. This reminds Allah's Messenger Muhammad (ﷺ) that Allah has perfect knowledge of the persecution that his people committed against him, and that He is able to stop them. However, He decided to give them respite, then give Muhammad (ﷺ) the victory and make him prevail over them, just as He gave Joseph victory and made him prevail over his brothers. Ibn Kathir: 2/454.\nThis verse ends with (But Allah is All-Knowing of what they did). Why?\nوَلَمَّا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُۥٓ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ حُكۡمٗا وَعِلۡمٗاۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٢٢\nAs for the light, knowledge, and wisdom, they are all indicated in this verse of Surat Yusuf, (And when he reached his prime, We gave him wisdom, and knowledge. This is how We reward those who do good). Ibn Taimyah: 4/22.\nEvery doer of good has a share in the light, knowledge and wisdom. Explain.\nوَلَمَّا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُۥٓ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ حُكۡمٗا وَعِلۡمٗاۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٢٢\nMentioning those who do good is an indication that he was rewarded with this blessing because he was a doer of good. Ibn Ashur: 12/248.\nState one of the benefits of being a good doer.\nwords\nوَأَجمَعُواThey determined and decided\nسَوَّلَتYour souls enticed you\nسَيَّارَةٌTravelers\nفَأَدلَى دَلوَهُHe lowered his bucket for water\nوَأَسَرُّوهُ بِضَاعَةًJoseph's brothers hid their kinship to him in order to sell him\nبَخسٍA low price\nمَثوَاهُHis stay"],[238,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nHumble yourself to Allah and seek refuge with Him from the trials of prosperity and adversity.\nShare a message in which you remind others not to expose a sinner who does not openly commit his sin, and the prohibition of spreading news of immorality among people.\nIdentify a gathering that reminds you of a sin and abandon it in pursuit of Allah's reward.\nguid\nRecalling the attributes of Allah, the Almighty, serves as a barrier between the servant and committing a sin.\nTurn to Allah during times of prosperity by obeying Him, so that he will respond and protect you during times of hardship.\nThe consequences of adultery and immorality are misery, loss and scandal.\nrefl\nوَرَٰوَدَتۡهُ ٱلَّتِي هُوَ فِي بَيۡتِهَا عَن نَّفۡسِهِۦ\nThis grave trial was harder for Joseph than the trial he went through at the hands of his brothers, and the patience with which he bore it brought a greater reward because it was patience based on a choice even though there were many reasons to commit the sin, but he gave precedence to the love of Allah over those reasons. As for the trial at the hands of his brothers, his patience, in that case, was the patience of one who had no other choice, as in the case of sickness and hardship that may befall a person with no choice on his part, and he has no option but to bear it patiently, willingly or unwillingly. Al-Saadi: 396.\nWhich trial is harder and more rewarding for Joseph (u): the trial with his brothers, or the one with his master's wife? Why?\nقَالَ مَعَاذَ ٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّهُۥ رَبِّيٓ أَحۡسَنَ مَثۡوَايَۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُفۡلِحُ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ ٢٣\n(The refuge of Allah), I seek refuge with Allah, and I hold firmly to Him from what you invited me to. Al-Baghawi: 2/449.\nSeeking refuge with Allah has a great impact in avoiding a sin. Explain.\nقَالَ مَعَاذَ ٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّهُۥ رَبِّيٓ أَحۡسَنَ مَثۡوَايَۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُفۡلِحُ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ ٢٣ وَلَقَدۡ هَمَّتۡ بِهِۦۖ وَهَمَّ بِهَا لَوۡلَآ أَن رَّءَا بُرۡهَٰنَ رَبِّهِۦۚ كَذَٰلِكَ لِنَصۡرِفَ عَنۡهُ ٱلسُّوٓءَ وَٱلۡفَحۡشَآءَۚ إِنَّهُۥ مِنۡ عِبَادِنَا ٱلۡمُخۡلَصِينَ ٢٤\nTo sum up, he mentioned reasons why he should not do this evil act, namely fear of Allah and observing the rights of his master who had shown him kindness, as well as protecting himself from wrongdoing, as those who do wrong never prosper. Moreover, Allah had blessed him with the proof of the faith that was in his heart, which dictated that he should comply with Allah's commands and avoid what He prohibited. All of that was because Allah had averted evil and shameful acts from him. Al-Saadi: 396.\nWhat are the reasons that helped Joseph (u) to avoid committing the sin?\nوَلَقَدۡ هَمَّتۡ بِهِۦۖ وَهَمَّ بِهَا لَوۡلَآ أَن رَّءَا بُرۡهَٰنَ رَبِّهِۦۚ كَذَٰلِكَ لِنَصۡرِفَ عَنۡهُ ٱلسُّوٓءَ وَٱلۡفَحۡشَآءَۚ إِنَّهُۥ مِنۡ عِبَادِنَا ٱلۡمُخۡلَصِينَ ٢٤\nAllah says, (and she certainly advanced towards him, and he would have inclined towards her, had he not seen a sign from his Lord), it is the proof of the faith that was in his heart, by which Allah had kept evil away from him, and rewarded him for a full good deed. Ibn Taimyah: 4/34.\nWhat was the sign that Joseph (u) saw?\nكَذَٰلِكَ لِنَصۡرِفَ عَنۡهُ ٱلسُّوٓءَ وَٱلۡفَحۡشَآءَۚ إِنَّهُۥ مِنۡ عِبَادِنَا ٱلۡمُخۡلَصِينَ ٢٤\nThis proves that sincerity prevents satan's control over a person, as Allah said, (This is how We kept evil and shameful acts away from him. Indeed, he was one of Our chosen servants). Ibn Taimyah: 4/36.\nHow do you infer from this verse that sincerity prevents satan's control over a person?\nوَٱسۡتَبَقَا ٱلۡبَابَ\nIf a person sees a place in which there is temptation and the means that lead to sin, he should get as far away as possible, so that he will be safe from sin. When the woman in whose house Joseph (u) was living wanted to seduce him, he tried to flee from her and ran to the door in order to save himself from her evil. Al-Saadi: 409.\nWhat lesson is learned from the fleeing of Joseph (u) from the place of sin?\nقَدۡ شَغَفَهَا حُبًّاۖ\nThis also warns against the type of love that may cause harm. The master's wife did what she did because of being alone with Joseph, which persisted until she attempted seduction and then told lies about him, and he was imprisoned for a long time because of her. Al-Saadi: 409.\nWhat is the risk of going along with love which is outside marriage?\nwords\nوَرَاوَدَتهُShe sought to seduce him\nهَيتَ لَكَCome here to me\nمَثوَايَMy stay, residence\nهَمَّت بِهِShe certainly advanced towards him\nوَهَمَّ بِهَاHe would have inclined towards her"],[239,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the plot of evil people.\nTurn to Allah and invoke Him for all of your concerns, for He is All-Hearing, All-Responsive.\nDo good to people, today, as much as you can, for it is an incentive for them to accept what you offer of truth and guidance.\nguid\nA sign of the people of truth is that they would prefer prison over disobeying Allah.\nIgnorance is not the lack of knowledge, rather it is falling into sins.\nThe suffering and distress in this worldly life is better than a quick pleasure followed by a punishment in the Hereafter.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ رَٰوَدتُّهُۥ عَن نَّفۡسِهِۦ فَٱسۡتَعۡصَمَۖ وَلَئِن لَّمۡ يَفۡعَلۡ مَآ ءَامُرُهُۥ لَيُسۡجَنَنَّ وَلَيَكُونٗا مِّنَ ٱلصَّٰغِرِينَ ٣٢ قَالَ رَبِّ ٱلسِّجۡنُ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِمَّا يَدۡعُونَنِيٓ إِلَيۡهِۖ وَإِلَّا تَصۡرِفۡ عَنِّي كَيۡدَهُنَّ أَصۡبُ إِلَيۡهِنَّ وَأَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡجَٰهِلِينَ ٣٣\n(But he abstained), he sought abstinence from what she wanted from him. (I might incline toward them), I might desire them. His speech here was in humility to Allah. Ibn Juzay: 1/415.\nWhen one is subjected to a trial, what should he do?\nقَالَ رَبِّ ٱلسِّجۡنُ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِمَّا يَدۡعُونَنِيٓ إِلَيۡهِۖ\nJoseph (u) chose prison over sin. This is what a person should do if he is tested with the choice of two things - either committing a sin or undergoing a worldly punishment; he should choose the worldly punishment over committing the sin which incurs a severe punishment in this world and the Hereafter. Hence one of the signs of faith is that a person hates to go back to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it, as he would hate to be thrown into the fire. Al-Saadi: 409.\nIf one has a choice of either committing a sin or undergoing a worldly punishment. Which one should he choose?\nقَالَ رَبِّ ٱلسِّجۡنُ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِمَّا يَدۡعُونَنِيٓ إِلَيۡهِۖ وَإِلَّا تَصۡرِفۡ عَنِّي كَيۡدَهُنَّ أَصۡبُ إِلَيۡهِنَّ وَأَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡجَٰهِلِينَ ٣٣\nThe words of Joseph (u) have two lessons, one of which is choosing prison and adversity over sins and disobedience. The second is invoking Allah to keep firm his heart on His religion, and direct it towards His obedience. If the heart is not firm, then it would incline towards those who enjoin committing sins, and become of the ignorant. So, within this invocation, there is a reliance upon Allah and seeking His help to keep firm the heart on faith and obedience; moreover, there is a display of patience in facing adversity, trial and harm as long as he maintains faith and obedience. Ibn Taimyah: 4/39.\nThere are great lessons in this verse, draw some of them.\nثُمَّ بَدَا لَهُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا رَأَوُاْ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لَيَسۡجُنُنَّهُۥ حَتَّىٰ حِينٖ ٣٥\nOverall, the circumstances that Joseph (u) went through were tenderness in violence, a blessing in disguise, a relief that came with hardship, a hope within despair, redemption after it was too late for deliverance. The predestined events rushed in violently, at times, and gently at others; but the vanquish and violence came with a great reward and less liability. Al-Biqai: 4/37.\nHow should the believer view the painful events destined by Allah?\nإِنَّا نَرَىٰكَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٣٦\nHe would visit a sick fellow prisoner and care for him. In gathering, he would make room for those who share the prison with him, and help them out when they needed something. Moreover, he strived in worship and prayed all night. Al-Baghawi: 2/461.\nJoseph (u) did good for others extensively that they came and ask him. What were some of the good things he did?\nقَالَ لَا يَأۡتِيكُمَا طَعَامٞ تُرۡزَقَانِهِۦٓ إِلَّا نَبَّأۡتُكُمَا بِتَأۡوِيلِهِۦ قَبۡلَ أَن يَأۡتِيَكُمَاۚ ذَٰلِكُمَا مِمَّا عَلَّمَنِي رَبِّيٓۚ إِنِّي تَرَكۡتُ مِلَّةَ قَوۡمٖ لَّا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَهُم بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ٣٧\nA sign of his good perception, when he saw that they were open to his call - as they thought positively of him and said to him, (We see you as one of those who do good), and they came to him so that he could interpret their dreams for them. He saw that they were eager to learn their interpretation from him - he saw that as an opportunity and made the most of it. So, he called them to Allah before interpreting their dreams. Al-Saadi: 410.\nFor one who calls others to Allah, he should have good judgement as to the best times to call others to Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nإِنِّي تَرَكۡتُ مِلَّةَ قَوۡمٖ لَّا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَهُم بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ٣٧\nJust as the person should be submissive to Allah at times of ease, he should also be submissive to Him at times of hardship. Joseph (u) kept calling people to Allah, and when he was put in prison he continued to do so. He called the two young men to affirm the Oneness of Allah, and he told them to give up ascribing partners to Him. Al-Saadi: 410.\nIs submission to Allah limited to the times of ease only?\nwords\nوَأَعتَدَتShe prepared\nمُتَّكَأًA banquet\nوَقَطَّعنَCut their hands\nحَاشَ لِلهِPerfect is Allah\nالصَّاغِرِينَThose who are humiliated\nأَصبُ إِلَيهِنَّI might incline toward them\nأَعصِرُ خَمرًاI am pressing grapes for wine"],[240,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nIn your supplication, say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with you lest I associate anything with you while I know it, and I seek your forgiveness for what I do not know.\"\nExpress your gratitude to Allah for the blessing of being guided to the truth, for many people are heedless of expressing this gratitude.\nBefore teaching someone, offer him some guidance, for many people are in dire need of guidance before learning.\nguid\nMake use of opportunities to call others to Allah as Joseph (u) did.\nA preacher should be lenient toward those whom he calls to Allah, and never acts with superiority or disdain for them.\nSeek refuge with Allah from satan's plot and deceit, for he is keen to distract you from your religious and worldly needs.\nrefl\nمَا كَانَ لَنَآ أَن نُّشۡرِكَ بِٱللَّهِ مِن شَيۡءٖۚ ذَٰلِكَ مِن فَضۡلِ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡنَا وَعَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَشۡكُرُونَ ٣٨\n(This is from Allah's favor upon us and upon people), this is part of His great blessings, favor and grace towards us and toward those whom Allah guides as He has guided us, for there is no greater blessing that Allah can bestow upon people than Islam and the true religion. Whoever accepts it and submits to Him is most fortunate, for he has attained the greatest blessings and the greatest virtues. Al-Saadi: 398.\nWhat are the greatest blessings of Allah upon you?\nمَا كَانَ لَنَآ أَن نُّشۡرِكَ بِٱللَّهِ مِن شَيۡءٖۚ ذَٰلِكَ مِن فَضۡلِ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡنَا وَعَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَشۡكُرُونَ ٣٨\nThis Tawhīd (Monotheism) -affirming that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone without partners- (this is from Allah's favor upon us), He has revealed it to us and ordained it on us, (and upon people), to whom He has sent us as callers to Tawhīd, (but most people are ungrateful), they do not admit Allah's favor and blessing of sending the Messengers to them. Ibn Kathir: 2/460.\nKnowing that most people are ungrateful inspires you to do something. What is it?\nوَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَشۡكُرُونَ ٣٨\n(But most people are ungrateful) for the blessing of Tawhīd and faith. Al-Qurtubi: 11/349.\nWhat is the great blessing for which people do not offer enough gratitude to Allah?\nإِنِ ٱلۡحُكۡمُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِ أَمَرَ أَلَّا تَعۡبُدُوٓاْ إِلَّآ إِيَّاهُۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلدِّينُ ٱلۡقَيِّمُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٠\nThe ruling and judgement belong to Allah, and His Messengers convey, on His behalf, to the people; therefore, their ruling is His, their ordain is His, and the obedience to them is that to Him. Whatever the Messenger ruled, enjoined and ordained as religious matters, then it is the duty of all people to follow and obey him because that is the rule of Allah upon His creation. Ibn Taimyah: 4/34.\nThe Messenger's rule is Allah's. Explain, in light of this verse.\nيَٰصَٰحِبَيِ ٱلسِّجۡنِ أَمَّآ أَحَدُكُمَا فَيَسۡقِي رَبَّهُۥ خَمۡرٗاۖ\nJoseph did not direct this speech at him, in order to lessen the grief of the other person. This is why he made his statement indirect. Ibn Kathir: 2/461.\nJoseph (u) did not indicate who would serve wine to his master and who would be crucified. Why?\nوَقَالَ لِلَّذِي ظَنَّ أَنَّهُۥ نَاجٖ مِّنۡهُمَا ٱذۡكُرۡنِي عِندَ رَبِّكَ فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ ذِكۡرَ رَبِّهِۦ فَلَبِثَ فِي ٱلسِّجۡنِ بِضۡعَ سِنِينَ ٤٢\n(So he remained in prison for several years), when Allah wanted to complete His decree and willed that Joseph (u) should be released from prison, He ordained means for that which caused Joseph (u) to be released, and to become prominent and attain high esteem; which was the king's dream. Al-Saadi: 398.\nExplain Allah's wisdom behind His will and destiny.\nوَقَالَ لِلَّذِي ظَنَّ أَنَّهُۥ نَاجٖ مِّنۡهُمَا ٱذۡكُرۡنِي عِندَ رَبِّكَ فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ ذِكۡرَ رَبِّهِۦ فَلَبِثَ فِي ٱلسِّجۡنِ بِضۡعَ سِنِينَ ٤٢\nIf a person finds himself faced with hardship and difficulty, there is nothing wrong with him seeking the help of anyone who has the ability to save him or to tell others about his situation. This is not regarded as complaining to other humans, because it is something normal; people usually seek one another's help. Hence, Joseph (u) said to the young man whom he thought would be saved, (mention me to your master). Al-Saadi: 410.\nDoes seeking people's help in what they are able to do contradict good faith?\nwords\nأَأَربَابٌ مُتَفَرِّقُونَIs worshiping many different lords?\nسُلطَانٍA proof\nرَبِّكَYour master, the king\nعِجَافٌBony and withered\nتَعبُرُونَInterpret"],[241,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nAsk a scholar about questions that you have been asked by people.\nAsk Allah to teach you, and open things for you as He did for Joseph (u).\nUse wit and permissible tricks to attain your right that is hard to recover.\nguid\nThe end result of righteousness is good, but that of disobedience and shameful acts is scandal.\nThe virtue and status of knowledge made the king bring Joseph (u) to his royal court.\nTruth will always prevail, even after the passage of time.\nrefl\nيُوسُفُ أَيُّهَا ٱلصِّدِّيقُ أَفۡتِنَا فِي سَبۡعِ بَقَرَٰتٖ سِمَانٖ يَأۡكُلُهُنَّ سَبۡعٌ عِجَافٞ\nHe described him as a (man of truth) since he knew him well when he was with him in prison. This is also a guidance for one who asks for a religious opinion \"fatwa\" to show respect for the scholar, \"mufti\", who delivers it. Al-Alusi: 12/604.\nWhat are some of the etiquettes when asking for an opinion from a mufti or a scholar?\nيُوسُفُ أَيُّهَا ٱلصِّدِّيقُ أَفۡتِنَا فِي سَبۡعِ بَقَرَٰتٖ سِمَانٖ يَأۡكُلُهُنَّ سَبۡعٌ عِجَافٞ\nKnowledge of dream interpretation is one of the branches of Islamic knowledge, and the person will be rewarded for learning and teaching it. Dream interpretation is like delivering a \"fatwa\" because the Arabic word used in the Quran’s text for (tell us) is \"give us a fatwa.\" Hence, it is not permissible to try to interpret dreams without knowledge. Al-Saadi: 410.\nWhat is Sharia rule on dream interpretation? How do you infer your answer?\nقَالَ تَزۡرَعُونَ سَبۡعَ سِنِينَ دَأَبٗا فَمَا حَصَدتُّمۡ فَذَرُوهُ فِي سُنۢبُلِهِۦٓ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا مِّمَّا تَأۡكُلُونَ ٤٧\nJoseph (u) told the interpretation of the dream, without criticizing the man for forgetting his request that he had made to him. Neither did he make a precondition that he be released before explaining the meaning. Ibn Kathir: 2/462.\nThe answer of Joseph (u) indicated his high morals and sound judgement. Explain.\nقَالَ تَزۡرَعُونَ سَبۡعَ سِنِينَ دَأَبٗا فَمَا حَصَدتُّمۡ فَذَرُوهُ فِي سُنۢبُلِهِۦٓ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا مِّمَّا تَأۡكُلُونَ ٤٧ ثُمَّ يَأۡتِي مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ذَٰلِكَ سَبۡعٞ شِدَادٞ يَأۡكُلۡنَ مَا قَدَّمۡتُمۡ لَهُنَّ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا مِّمَّا تُحۡصِنُونَ ٤٨\nWith his interpretation of the King's dream, Joseph (u) included valuable guidance for rationing and preserving the food supply to suit the best interest of the community. Ibn Ashur: 12/286.\nJoseph (u) included guidance with his interpretation of the king's dream. Explain.\nوَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلِكُ ٱئۡتُونِي بِهِۦۖ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُ ٱلرَّسُولُ قَالَ ٱرۡجِعۡ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ فَسۡـَٔلۡهُ مَا بَالُ ٱلنِّسۡوَةِ ٱلَّٰتِي قَطَّعۡنَ أَيۡدِيَهُنَّۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي بِكَيۡدِهِنَّ عَلِيمٞ ٥٠\nJoseph (u) did not mention the chief minister's wife -showing gratitude to him and covering up the fault of his wife, rather he mentioned the women who cut their hands. Ibn Juzay: 1/418.\nJoseph's (u) request to ask the women before leaving prison indicated his wisdom and forbearance. Explain.\nوَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلِكُ ٱئۡتُونِي بِهِۦۖ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُ ٱلرَّسُولُ قَالَ ٱرۡجِعۡ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ فَسۡـَٔلۡهُ مَا بَالُ ٱلنِّسۡوَةِ ٱلَّٰتِي قَطَّعۡنَ أَيۡدِيَهُنَّۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي بِكَيۡدِهِنَّ عَلِيمٞ ٥٠\nIbn Atiyah said: Joseph (u) was concerned that when he gets out of prison to be honored by the king who would be silent about his case and pardons him, then people would always see him as the guilty of seducing his master's wife but was freed by the king. So, he wanted to assert his innocence, and regain his high status of chasteness and goodness; then leave the prison to be honored. That is why he said to messenger: Return to your master and ask him what is the case of the women. Al-Qurtubi: 11/372.\nExplain the wisdom and endurance behind Joseph's (u) request to re-open his case.\nوَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلِكُ ٱئۡتُونِي بِهِۦۖ\nThis story highlights the virtue of knowledge, namely knowledge of rulings, laws, dream interpretation, management and education; it indicates that knowledge is superior to having a good image, even if it is as beautiful as Joseph was. Because of his beauty, Joseph went through all these trials and was imprisoned, but because of his knowledge, he attained honor and high status, and was established in the land. All that is good in this world and in the Hereafter is the result and consequences of knowledge. Al-Saadi: 410.\nIn light of the story of Joseph (u), compare between knowledge and outer beauty.\nwords\nأَضغَاثُA mixture [of false dreams]\nأُمَّةٍAfter a time\nدَأَبًاConsecutively\nتُحصِنُونَYou preserve, store\nيَعصرونThey press succulent crops due to abundance\nحَاشَ لِلهِPerfect is Allah\nحَصحَصَ الحَقّThe truth has come to light"],[242,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil of your soul, and from the evil and shirk of the devil.\nRecall a situation that happened to you, then identify the mistakes you made and ask Allah for forgiveness.\nBe kind to one of your brothers or relatives.\nguid\nAdmitting your sins is the first step to receiving forgiveness, and it is a sign of sincere repentance and turning back to Allah.\nDo justice to the oppressed and help them. Bring closer the truthful and the trustworthy, even if he is weak or a stranger.\nWith patience, the glory comes after humiliation and injustice.\nrefl\nوَمَآ أُبَرِّئُ نَفۡسِيٓۚ إِنَّ ٱلنَّفۡسَ لَأَمَّارَةُۢ بِٱلسُّوٓءِ إِلَّا مَا رَحِمَ رَبِّيٓۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٥٣\nIt is said that human souls are three types: (A persistent enjoiner of evil), which tends toward following its whim because of sins and wrongdoings. (A self-reproaching soul), which commits sins and repents, so it has good and evil, but when it does evil, it reverts and repents, therefore, it is called \"reproaching\" since it reproaches itself and wavers between good and evil. (A tranquil soul), which likes to do good deeds, wants them, and detests evil deeds; and that became its demeanor and habit. Ibn Taimyah: 4/45.\nWhat are the types of human souls?\nوَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلِكُ ٱئۡتُونِي بِهِۦٓ أَسۡتَخۡلِصۡهُ لِنَفۡسِيۖ فَلَمَّا كَلَّمَهُۥ قَالَ إِنَّكَ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ لَدَيۡنَا مَكِينٌ أَمِينٞ ٥٤\nIndeed, you are today established [in position] and trusted), this answer from the king indicates that Joseph (u) had spoken to him in a wise and eloquent manner. So, when the king witnessed his articulate speech and original views, he realized that he was worthy of his trust and of being around him. Ibn Ashur: 13/7.\nWhat is the reason for the king's saying to Joseph (u): (Indeed, you are today established [in position] and trusted)?\nقَالَ ٱجۡعَلۡنِي عَلَىٰ خَزَآئِنِ ٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ إِنِّي حَفِيظٌ عَلِيمٞ ٥٥\nProphet Muhammad (ﷺ) had censured the idea of one requesting to be appointed to an official position; however, the request of Joseph (u), (Appoint me over the storehouses of the land) was a way for him to call them to Allah, act justly among the people, eliminate injustice, and do good which they [would not], even though they were not aware of his qualification, but he knew through his interpretation of the dream how the conditions of the people would turn out, which made the difference between this case and what was censured by the Prophet (ﷺ). Ibn Taimyah: 4/55-56.\nHow did Joseph (u) request to be appointed even though it is censured to do that?\nقَالَ ٱجۡعَلۡنِي عَلَىٰ خَزَآئِنِ ٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ إِنِّي حَفِيظٌ عَلِيمٞ ٥٥\nThis verse proves that it is permissible for one to talk about his knowledge and virtue. Al-Mawardi said: Talking about the traits of oneself is not permitted with all traits in general, but limited to traits that are relative to the situation, or linked to justifying earning, but forbidden for everything else because it is a display of self-admiration and show. If a virtuous man refrains from it, it will be more suitable to his virtue, however, the condition in which Joseph (u) was necessitated his statement, and the fact that he was hoping to be united with his family. Al-Qurtubi: 11/386.\nIs it permissible for a person to speak favorably and praise himself?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوسُفَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ يَتَبَوَّأُ مِنۡهَا حَيۡثُ يَشَآءُۚ نُصِيبُ بِرَحۡمَتِنَا مَن نَّشَآءُۖ وَلَا نُضِيعُ أَجۡرَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٥٦\n(We do not allow to be lost the reward of those who do good), Ibn Abbas and Wahb said: This refers to those who are patient, since he was patient at the bottom of the well, when he was taken as a slave, when he entered the prison and when he was called to do forbidden action by a woman. Al-Qurtubi: 11/390.\nWhat are the types of patience that Joseph (u) displayed?\nوَلَأَجۡرُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ خَيۡرٞ لِّلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَكَانُواْ يَتَّقُونَ ٥٧\nIt is through piety that both major and minor sins are abandoned, and through perfect faith that the heart believes in what Allah has commanded it to believe, followed by the deeds of the heart and physical actions, both obligatory and recommended. Al-Saadi: 401.\nWhy are piety and faith important to reach the reward of the Hereafter?\nوَقَالَ لِفِتۡيَٰنِهِ ٱجۡعَلُواْ بِضَٰعَتَهُمۡ فِي رِحَالِهِمۡ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَعۡرِفُونَهَآ إِذَا ٱنقَلَبُوٓاْ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهِمۡ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَرۡجِعُونَ ٦٢\nIt is said that he wanted to show them his generosity by returning their trading goods, and give them an incentive to come back through benevolence. (So that they might know it), so that they may recognize our caring for them. Al-Baghawi: 2/475.\nShed some light on the generosity of Joseph (u) toward his brothers and his keenness to see them?\nwords\nلأَمَّارَةٌ بِالسُّوءِA persistent enjoiner of evil\nأَستَخلِصهُI will appoint him exclusively for myself\nمَكِينٌWell established in position\nيَتَبَوَّأُHe settles\nجَهَّزَهُم بِجَهَازِهِمHe furnished them with their supplies\nسَنُرَاوِدُWe will attempt to persuade his father\nرِحَالِهِمTheir saddlebags"],[243,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nMaintain the remembrance of Allah (Athkar) after daily prayers; for they are a protection from evil eye and magic.\nFind a brother in need and help him out.\nRecord the traits of Joseph (u) and the steps he used to resolve his problem with his brothers, then learn from that how to settle one of your big problems.\nguid\nA wise man should be wary of the harm caused by the evil eye and envy, and he takes protective measures but without exaggeration.\nStrive in adopting means to reach the end result but do not rely on them, rather rely on Allah Whose all matters are in His Hands.\nObey your parents, consult with them, and ask for their permission, for what they request you to do is for your good.\nrefl\nقَالَ هَلۡ ءَامَنُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ إِلَّا كَمَآ أَمِنتُكُمۡ عَلَىٰٓ أَخِيهِ مِن قَبۡلُ فَٱللَّهُ خَيۡرٌ حَٰفِظٗاۖ وَهُوَ أَرۡحَمُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ٦٤\nNegative assumption -when there is circumstantial evidence that points to that- is not objectionable nor prohibited. Al-Saadi: 411\nWhen is negative assumption forbidden?\nفَٱللَّهُ خَيۡرٌ حَٰفِظٗاۖ وَهُوَ أَرۡحَمُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ٦٤\nJacob (u) says that Allah's guardianship is better than yours, and He is the most merciful of the merciful. Al-Baghawi: 2/476.\nJacob (u) displayed sure faith in Allah. How?\nوَقَالَ يَٰبَنِيَّ لَا تَدۡخُلُواْ مِنۢ بَابٖ وَٰحِدٖ وَٱدۡخُلُواْ مِنۡ أَبۡوَٰبٖ مُّتَفَرِّقَةٖۖ\nThis verse proves taking precaution against evil eye, as evil eye is real. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The evil eye is capable of putting a man into his grave, and putting a camel in a cooking pot.\" And when seeking refuge, he would say, \"I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from every devil and scourge and every harmful eye,\" which proves thereof. Al-Qurtubi: 11/399.\nHow does the believer take precaution against evil eye?\nوَقَالَ يَٰبَنِيَّ لَا تَدۡخُلُواْ مِنۢ بَابٖ وَٰحِدٖ وَٱدۡخُلُواْ مِنۡ أَبۡوَٰبٖ مُّتَفَرِّقَةٖۖ وَمَآ أُغۡنِي عَنكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن شَيۡءٍۖ إِنِ\nThis verse proves that the believer should warn his brother against harm, and offer him guidance to what keeps him safe and secure, as religion is sincere advice, and a Muslim is a brother of another Muslim. Al-Qurtubi: 11/403.\nWhat should you do if you fear for your brother's safety?\nوَقَالَ يَٰبَنِيَّ لَا تَدۡخُلُواْ مِنۢ بَابٖ وَٰحِدٖ وَٱدۡخُلُواْ مِنۡ أَبۡوَٰبٖ مُّتَفَرِّقَةٖۖ وَمَآ أُغۡنِي عَنكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن شَيۡءٍۖ إِنِ ٱلۡحُكۡمُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِۖ عَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡتُۖ وَعَلَيۡهِ فَلۡيَتَوَكَّلِ ٱلۡمُتَوَكِّلُونَ ٦٧\nHe wanted to teach them reliance on the grace and success from Allah while adopting the usual apparent means; showing their disciplined manner with the One Who created the means and decreed events in a subtle way. Ibn Ashur: 13/21.\nDoes adopting the means for achieving a certain result contradicts reliance on Allah? Explain in light of this verse.\nمَّا كَانَ يُغۡنِي عَنۡهُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن شَيۡءٍ إِلَّا حَاجَةٗ فِي نَفۡسِ يَعۡقُوبَ قَضَىٰهَاۚ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَذُو عِلۡمٖ لِّمَا عَلَّمۡنَٰهُ\nThis was the result of compassion and love for his children; therefore, by giving them this advice, he put his mind at rest. This was not due to any lack of knowledge on his part, for he was one of the noble Messengers and devoted scholars. Hence, Allah says of him, (And he was indeed a man of knowledge), which indicates that he had great knowledge. Al-Saadi: 402.\nAfter mentioning that Jacob's (u) plan did not avail them, Allah says, (And he was indeed a man of knowledge). Why?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَذُو عِلۡمٖ لِّمَا عَلَّمۡنَٰهُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٦٨\n(He was indeed a man of knowledge), he did what he did out of knowledge, not ignorance. (Because of what We had taught him) due to our teaching of him. It is said that he practiced what he knew. Sufyan said: Whoever does not practice what he knows is not considered a scholar. Al-Baghawi: 2/503.\nWhen can one be considered a scholar?\nwords\nمَا نَبغِيWhat more could we ask for?\nوَنَمِيرُWe will obtain more food\nآوَىHe took his brother to himself\nفلا تَبتَئِسDo not grieve"],[244,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nRead the story of Joseph (u) in one of the Quran interpretation books to gain more knowledge on this subject.\nSupplicate Allah, the Almighty, seek Him and stand in need of Him, so that He may grant you knowledge and understanding.\nStarting today, practice to suppress your anger as much as possible.\nguid\nThis is a manifestation of Allah's best arrangement of matters for His allies.\nWhen Allah loves a servant, He grants him understanding and knowledge.\nWhen the servant realizes that Allah, the Almighty, knows His servants; their plans, deceptions and what they claim, people's words become meaningless to him, and he becomes proud and sufficed in Allah.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّا جَهَّزَهُم بِجَهَازِهِمۡ جَعَلَ ٱلسِّقَايَةَ فِي رَحۡلِ أَخِيهِ ثُمَّ أَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ أَيَّتُهَا ٱلۡعِيرُ إِنَّكُمۡ لَسَٰرِقُونَ ٧٠\nIt is permissible to use tricks to attain one's rights, and knowing hidden ways of achieving one's aims is something that is praiseworthy. What is prohibited is using tricks to avoid obligations or commit prohibited acts. Al-Saadi: 411.\nIn light of this verse, what are the permitted tricks? What are the forbidden ones?\nفَلَمَّا جَهَّزَهُم بِجَهَازِهِمۡ جَعَلَ ٱلسِّقَايَةَ فِي رَحۡلِ أَخِيهِ ثُمَّ أَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ أَيَّتُهَا ٱلۡعِيرُ إِنَّكُمۡ لَسَٰرِقُونَ ٧٠\nIn calling them (thieves), two justifications were made, the first: It is said that Joseph's intention was hinting to the fact that they stole him from his father by taking him away using a ploy and betrayed their father, and a betrayer is called a thief. This is a widely used expression where even the betrayers among government workers are called thieves. Second: The announcer who called out did that without Joseph's (u) directive. Ibn Taimyah: 4/57.\nJoseph's brothers were called (thieves) even though they were not. How?\nكَذَٰلِكَ كِدۡنَا لِيُوسُفَۖ مَا كَانَ لِيَأۡخُذَ أَخَاهُ فِي دِينِ ٱلۡمَلِكِ إِلَّآ أَن يَشَآءَ ٱللَّهُۚ\nHaving described how Joseph accomplished what he wanted to do of keeping his brother with him in such a way that his other brothers would not realize it, Allah says, (Thus did We plan for Joseph), We made easy for him this plan which enabled him to achieve something that was not blameworthy. Al-Saadi: 402.\nIf Allah decrees good for His allies, none can withhold it. Explain in light of this verse.\nنَرۡفَعُ دَرَجَٰتٖ مَّن نَّشَآءُۗ وَفَوۡقَ كُلِّ ذِي عِلۡمٍ عَلِيمٞ ٧٦\nMeaning: Raising in knowledge, which is inferred by the next verse (but over all those endowed with knowledge is the All-Knowing (Allah)). That is, above each knowledgeable person is another (in knowledge), or Allah, the Almighty. Ibn Juzay: 1/422.\nIn this verse, the degrees are interpreted as knowledge. Why?\nنَرۡفَعُ دَرَجَٰتٖ مَّن نَّشَآءُۗ\nMeaning: Raising the degrees through knowledge and faith. Al-Qurtubi: 11/417.\nWhat are the things that raise a servant higher in degrees?\nوَفَوۡقَ كُلِّ ذِي عِلۡمٍ عَلِيمٞ ٧٦\nIbn Abbas (t) said: Above each knowledgeable person is another (in knowledge), and so on until the ultimate knowledge ends up with Allah, so, He is above all those who have knowledge. Al-Baghawi: 2/481.\nDescribe the vastness of Allah's knowledge?\nقَالُوٓاْ إِن يَسۡرِقۡ فَقَدۡ سَرَقَ أَخٞ لَّهُۥ مِن قَبۡلُۚ فَأَسَرَّهَا يُوسُفُ فِي نَفۡسِهِۦ وَلَمۡ يُبۡدِهَا لَهُمۡۚ قَالَ أَنتُمۡ شَرّٞ مَّكَانٗاۖ وَٱللَّهُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا تَصِفُونَ ٧٧\n(And Allah is most knowing of what you describe), Allah knows that what you are saying is a lie. It is said that Joseph's (u) brothers were not Prophets at that time. Al-Qurtubi: 9/228.\nA lie was ascribed to Joseph's (u) brothers even though it is said that they were Prophets. How?\nwords\nالعِيرُThe caravan\nصُوَاعَA measuring bowl\nزَعِيمٌA guarantor\nدِينِ المَلِكِThe king's law, which does not enslave a thief"],[245,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nReflect on the meanings of the Names of Allah that were mentioned in the words of Jacob (u) in this story, and how they were the reason behind his steadfastness.\nToday, be sure to say this supplication when leaving your house—which includes seeking refuge from injustice—and say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You lest I stray or be led astray, or slip or made to slip, or cause injustice, or suffer injustice, or behave foolishly, or be treated foolishly.\"\nRemind, give advice, and pledge to do good with your brothers, as Joseph's eldest brother did with his brothers.\nguid\nTurn to Allah first before anyone else, especially in times of calamity.\nWeeping and sorrow do not contradict sure faith and steadfastness.\nLoving and yearning for one's children do not contradict faith, and it is nothing to be ashamed of for men, but it may be a subject of a trial.\nrefl\nقَالَ مَعَاذَ ٱللَّهِ أَن نَّأۡخُذَ إِلَّا مَن وَجَدۡنَا مَتَٰعَنَا عِندَهُۥٓ\nThe one who wants to give a wrong impression to someone else in order to avoid disclosing something that he does not want to disclose may use vague words and actions that will prevent him from telling lies, as Joseph did when he put the measuring bowl in his brother's saddlebag, then brought it out in order to give the impression that he was a thief, but there was no proof except circumstantial evidence that would give a wrong impression to his brothers. After that he said: (Allah forbid that we should take except the one with whom we found our property) and did not say, \"the man who stole our property\". Al-Saadi: 411.\nHow did Joseph (u) evade lying when he wanted to take his brother?\nوَمَا شَهِدۡنَآ إِلَّا بِمَا عَلِمۡنَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِلۡغَيۡبِ حَٰفِظِينَ ٨١\nThis verse entails that it is admissible to testify in accordance with available knowledge, as testimony is tied to the knowledge of events intellectually and from the standpoint of Sharia, so, do not accept any testimony except from one who knows. Al-Qurtubi: 11/426.\nWhat do you think of one who testifies to things of which he has no knowledge? Is that permissible?\nفَصَبۡرٞ جَمِيلٌۖ عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَأۡتِيَنِي بِهِمۡ جَمِيعًاۚ\nIn the Quran, Allah mentions gracious patience, gracious forgiveness, and gracious avoidance. Gracious patience is patience without complaint, gracious avoidance is avoidance without hurt, and gracious forgiveness is forgiveness without blame. Ibn Taimyah: 4/63-64.\nWhat is meant by: gracious patience, gracious forgiveness and gracious avoidance?\nفَصَبۡرٞ جَمِيلٌۖ عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَأۡتِيَنِي بِهِمۡ جَمِيعًاۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٨٣\nIt is Allah's way that when a hardship reaches its peak, a great relief becomes imminent. It seemed that when Jacob (u) saw the intensity of the trial, his hope in Allah's relief became stronger, so he said what he said. Al-Alusi: 13/51.\nThe imminence of relief has a sign which is known by pious scholars. What is it?\nوَقَالَ يَٰٓأَسَفَىٰ عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ وَٱبۡيَضَّتۡ عَيۡنَاهُ مِنَ ٱلۡحُزۡنِ فَهُوَ كَظِيمٞ ٨٤\nThis verse is quoted as evidence that it is permissible to display sorrow and weeping when encountering calamities, while abstaining from that is not mandatory since very few people can withhold their emotions when facing disasters. In Sahih Al-Bukhari and Muslim, Anas (t) narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) wept over the death of his son, Ibrahim, and said: \"The eyes are shedding tears and the heart is grieved, but we will not say except what pleases our Lord. O Ibrahim, Indeed, we are grieved by your departure.\" The prohibited actions are: Slapping faces and chests, and tearing clothes. Al-Alusi: 13/53.\nWhen facing calamities, what actions are recommended, lawful and unlawful?\nقَالَ إِنَّمَآ أَشۡكُواْ بَثِّي وَحُزۡنِيٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَأَعۡلَمُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٨٦\nMeaning: I complain to Allah only, not to you or anyone else. The Arabic word used for (suffering) denotes extreme sorrow. (And I know from Allah that which you do not know), I know enough of His kindness, compassion and mercy that which makes me fully trusting in Him, and strengthen my hope in Him. Ibn Juzay: 1/425.\nWhat did Jacob (u) mean by saying, (And I know from Allah that which you do not know)?\nقَالَ إِنَّمَآ أَشۡكُواْ بَثِّي وَحُزۡنِيٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ\nComplaining to Allah is not contrary to patience; rather what is contrary to that is complaining to people. Al-Saadi: 411.\nWhen does complaining contradict patience?\nwords\nاستَيأَسُواThey had despaired\nأَبرَحَI leave\nكَظِيمٌHe was suppressive due to his sorrow\nتَفتَأُYou will not cease"],[246,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nRecall a calamity that has befallen the Muslims, then compare it to Allah's attribute, the Most Capable, then you will live with optimism.\nAsk Allah to grant you piety and patience, for they are the path to doing good.\nIdentify a problem that occurred between you and one of your relatives, and make a decision to forgive him for the sake of Allah, the Almighty, so that you be closer to Allah's Mercy.\nguid\nBeware of despairing of Allah's mercy and His forgiveness of your sin, as He is the Most Merciful, Most Generous.\nThree traits of Joseph (u) brought him the best outcome, they are piety, patience, and doing good.\nOne of the qualities of Prophets is forgiving those who wronged them. Do not be satisfied with merely forgiving someone who has wronged you, but also invoke Allah for him to benefit him in this life and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nيَٰبَنِيَّ ٱذۡهَبُواْ فَتَحَسَّسُواْ مِن يُوسُفَ وَأَخِيهِ وَلَا تَاْيۡـَٔسُواْ مِن رَّوۡحِ ٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يَاْيۡـَٔسُ مِن رَّوۡحِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٨٧\nHope makes a person strive to achieve what he wishes for, whereas despair leads to apathy and giving up. Al-Saadi: 404.\nWhat is the benefit of trusting in Allah, and not despair of His mercy?\nإِنَّهُۥ لَا يَاْيۡـَٔسُ مِن رَّوۡحِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٨٧\nDespair is a trait of the disbelievers because it is caused by denying the Lordship of Allah, or by the [ignorance] of the Attributes of Allah such as His Capability, His Bounty and His Mercy. Ibn Juzay: 1/425.\nWhy is despair a trait of the disbelievers?\nفَلَمَّا دَخَلُواْ عَلَيۡهِ قَالُواْ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلۡعَزِيزُ مَسَّنَا وَأَهۡلَنَا ٱلضُّرُّ وَجِئۡنَا بِبِضَٰعَةٖ مُّزۡجَىٰةٖ فَأَوۡفِ لَنَا ٱلۡكَيۡلَ وَتَصَدَّقۡ عَلَيۡنَآۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُتَصَدِّقِينَ ٨٨ قَالَ هَلۡ عَلِمۡتُم مَّا فَعَلۡتُم بِيُوسُفَ وَأَخِيهِ إِذۡ أَنتُمۡ جَٰهِلُونَ ٨٩\nWhen they complained, he was moved by their situation and revealed his identity to them. Ibn Juzay: 1/425.\nShed some light on the effect of a good speech on the souls, and how it can change views.\nإِنَّهُۥ مَن يَتَّقِ وَيَصۡبِرۡ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجۡرَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٩٠\nMeaning: He fears Allah and bears patiently with trials and against committing sins. (Allah will not let the reward of those who do good to go to waste), those who remain patient with His trial and in His obedience. Al-Qurtubi: 11/443.\nWhen does the servant reach the honor in this worldly life and the Hereafter?\nقَالَ لَا تَثۡرِيبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡيَوۡمَۖ يَغۡفِرُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۖ وَهُوَ أَرۡحَمُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ٩٢\nHe dropped his right by saying, (no blame will there be upon you today), then he invoked Allah to forgive them for violating his right. Ibn Juzay: 1/426.\nIn this verse, a great example of the high morals of Prophets. Explain.\nقَالَ لَا تَثۡرِيبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡيَوۡمَۖ يَغۡفِرُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۖ وَهُوَ أَرۡحَمُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ٩٢\nMeaning: No reproach on you today, and I will not mention your misdeed to you after today. Al-Baghawi: 2/494.\nJoseph (u) had forgiven his brothers to a great extent. How?\nٱذۡهَبُواْ بِقَمِيصِي هَٰذَا فَأَلۡقُوهُ عَلَىٰ وَجۡهِ أَبِي يَأۡتِ بَصِيرٗا\nJacob's sorrow began with Joseph's shirt which was stained with false blood, so Joseph (u) picked his shirt from among his items to be the beginning of his father's joy. He wanted his shirt to be a source of joy after it was a cause for sorrow to his father. Al-Alusi: 14/103.\nWhy did Joseph (u) pick his shirt from among his items?\nwords\nوَلاَ تَيأَسُواDo not despair\nبِبِضَاعَةٍ مُزجَاةٍSome goods of scanty worth\nلاَ تَثرِيبَNo blame will there be upon you\nفَصَلَتِ العِيرُWhen the caravan departed from Egypt\nتُفَنِّدُونِYou think me weakened in mind"]])